WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
[Man]: Give me an advice as a parent

00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:04.995
[Gary]: I can tell you, yea.
I can tell you what not to do

00:00:05.845 --> 00:00:08.785
[Reporter]: As the the US college admission bribery allegations continue

00:00:08.785 --> 00:00:11.825
to expand, they include high profile celebries

00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:13.305
and wealthy families.

00:00:13.895 --> 00:00:16.855
[Gary]: Going to Harvard or Stanford or Yale

00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:20.285
is a badge that people walk around proudly

00:00:20.955 --> 00:00:23.925
and they're fu*king their kids up.

00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:26.975
I love how everybody's focused on how these parents f*ck other kids

00:00:26.975 --> 00:00:27.475
that couldn't get in

00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:28.680
[Man]: There are a lot of advantages

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.180
for rich people

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.960
to make it an uneven playing field

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.000
[Journalist]: Kids who belive that they're boxed out because of social standing

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.580
[Man]: Oportunity 101

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.500
[Gary]: No, no. They totally f*ck their own children in perpetuity

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.900
you have a kid who knows they're not good enough and that mommy and daddy buy their way in. that is broken forever

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.260
for sure

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.440
your parents don't believe in you

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.640
These parents actually care more about other people's opinions

00:00:53.645 --> 00:00:56.675
about their kids more than they do with the mental well being

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.860
of their own children

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.535
I f a parents thinks that a kid's acomplishment is a reflection of them

00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:05.725
now you have a disconnect, now you're not a parent and a child

00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:07.735
you're a person with a product

00:01:08.765 --> 00:01:11.795
The way we do school today and the way we structure our kids for success

00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:13.695
is so broken worldwide

00:01:14.385 --> 00:01:17.295
It doesn't matter what you want for your kids

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.155
the only thing you should want for your kids is happiness

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.480
and the best way for somebody to be happy si for them to be self aware

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.185
your job is to reverse engineer them

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:26.985
at all times

00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:29.075
your job is to watch them

00:01:29.075 --> 00:01:32.525
what their intrests are, what their desires are, what their talents are

00:01:32.595 --> 00:01:35.495
and communicate to them on their level

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.945
not on your expectations or ambitions

00:01:37.945 --> 00:01:40.620
lean into the things that make them happy

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.580
[rewind]

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.540
[Man]: Give me an advice as a parent

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.235
[Gary]: I can tell you what not to do

00:01:48.235 --> 00:01:49.335
you shouldn't buy

00:01:49.335 --> 00:01:51.835
you shouldn't buy your kid's way into fancy colleges

